-- Destination enrichment.
--
-- Adds the reader-facing detail that turns a listing into a guide: what you
-- actually see, what the habitat is made of, what to wear, the short do/never
-- do rules shown in the etiquette panel, and the conservation context.
--
-- Everything here is written to be verifiable: water temperatures are anchored
-- to a season, rules are split into do and never-do, and the conservation note
-- names the body or programme that does the work.

-- ---------- regions ----------
update regions set
  highlights = v.highlights::text[],
  wetsuit_note = v.wetsuit_note,
  rules_do = v.rules_do::text[],
  rules_avoid = v.rules_avoid::text[]
from (values
 ('california',
  '{"Orange garibaldi in the kelp forests of Catalina","Summer leopard shark aggregations at La Jolla Shores","Marine reserves covering most of the Southern California coast"}',
  'A 3mm full suit most of the year: the water sits around 60-64F (16-18C). A 2mm shorty is enough from July to September, when it reaches 68F (20C).',
  '{"Stay inside the marine reserve boundaries","Keep your hands off the kelp and the rock","Pack out everything you carry in"}',
  '{"Do not take any marine life, including urchins, abalone and rockfish","Do not feed fish or sea lions","Do not swim in a closed rookery"}'),
 ('california/san-diego',
  '{"Garibaldi fish grazing in the kelp at La Jolla Cove","Leopard sharks in the warm shallows from June to October","The La Jolla Shores tidewalk along a protected kelp bed"}',
  'A 3mm full suit for most visits: La Jolla water runs 62-66F (16-19C). From July to September a 2mm shorty is usually enough.',
  '{"Walk on the sand at the tidewalk and step off it to swim","Shuffle your feet when you walk on the sand","Keep at least 10 ft (3 m) from leopard sharks"}',
  '{"Do not swim off the Scripps pier: rips run around the pilings","Do not touch or stand on the kelp bed","Do not take abalone, urchins or any marine life"}'),
 ('california/catalina-island',
  '{"Kelp forests that run from the beach into the channel","Sea lions hauled out on the rocks at Casino Point and Camp Cactus","A marine reserve that covers the whole south end of the island"}',
  'A 3mm full suit is the standard here: the Catalina Channel runs 60-64F (16-18C) most of the year. Snorkelers wear one even on a calm July day.',
  '{"Keep well back from resting sea lions and seals","Stay on the trail at Little Eggs Beach","Use reef shoes for the rock entry"}',
  '{"Do not enter the closed marine mammal rookery at Little Eggs Beach","Do not take marine life: the whole island is a no-take reserve","Do not swim alone; the channel builds current quickly"}'),
 ('florida',
  '{"The only living coral barrier reef in the continental United States","Manatee and spring runs that hold 68-72F all year","Sea turtles nesting on uncrowded beaches from May to October"}',
  'Ocean: a 3mm shorty or rash guard from November to March, when the Gulf drops to 70-75F (21-24C). Springs: skin or a 1mm suit, because the water never drops below about 68F (20C).',
  '{"Check for stingrays and shuffle your feet in shallow sand","Keep 10 ft (3 m) from turtles and manatees","Fly a dive flag on any boat snorkel in state waters"}',
  '{"Do not take coral, sponges or any marine life","Do not stand on coral","Do not feed wildlife or block a turtle''s path to the surface"}'),
 ('florida/south-florida',
  '{"Coral patch reefs in Biscayne National Park by boat","A natural three-tier reef 100 yards off a street-end beach in Lauderdale","The reef tract that starts at the sand and runs 21 miles off the Keys"}',
  'A 3mm shorty from November to March, when the water sits at 72-75F (22-24C). A rash guard is enough from May to October.',
  '{"Fly a dive flag on any boat snorkel","Keep a wide berth from the boat channel","Stay inside the marked swim zones in Biscayne National Park"}',
  '{"Do not take coral or marine life anywhere in the Keys reef tract","Do not touch the wrecks or the trail markers","Do not swim in the marked channels"}'),
 ('florida/miami',
  '{"Biscayne National Park reefs with wild coral and large fish","A shallow, sandy bottom at Crandon Park for beginners","Patch reefs and wrecks a short boat ride from the city"}',
  'A 3mm shorty or rash guard is enough from May to October. From December to March the water drops to 72-75F (22-24C) and many snorkelers wear one.',
  '{"Check the tide and wind before you leave the beach","Use the free three-hour parking passes at Crandon Park","Watch the channel markers and stay on the ocean side"}',
  '{"Do not take shells or coral","Do not feed the fish","Do not swim in the inlet or the marina channel"}'),
 ('florida/lauderdale-by-the-sea',
  '{"A three-tier natural reef that starts about 100 yards from a street-end beach","The 2002 Shipwreck Snorkel Trail over the broken-up SS Copenhagen","Turtles and schooling fish on a reef most people can reach from shore"}',
  'A 3mm shorty from November to March, when the water sits near 72F (22C). Most people snorkel without one from May to October.',
  '{"Look for the yellow marker buoys and keep the trail in sight","Watch for boats and give divers room at the reef","Park legally and use the beach portal at the end of Datura Avenue"}',
  '{"Do not touch the wreck pieces, the anchor or the cannon","Do not take any artefact or marine life","Do not enter the marked channel"}'),
 ('florida/florida-keys',
  '{"The only reef in the continental US that starts at the sand","A 21-mile reef tract running from John Pennekamp to the edge of the shelf","Loggerhead turtles nesting on the Keys beaches"}',
  'A 3mm shorty from November to March, when the water is 72-75F (22-24C); a rash guard or skin from May to October, when it reaches 85F (29C).',
  '{"Fly a dive flag: it is required by state law","Stay on the marked snorkel trail at John Pennekamp","Carry water, sunscreen and a cover-up, because the reef gives no shade"}',
  '{"Do not spearfish or take coral anywhere in the Keys sanctuary","Do not touch the Seven Mile Bridge stumps or cut off barnacles","Do not swim in the Dry Tortugas moat"}'),
 ('florida/florida-springs',
  '{"Water that holds 68-72F all year because it never sees sunlight","Wild manatees in the colder months","Clear spring runs you can swim for a mile"}',
  'None needed. The water sits at 68-72F (20-22C) all year, so a swimsuit is more comfortable than a wetsuit. Use a 1mm suit only if you are cold-sensitive.',
  '{"Use a float and a snorkel in the spring runs","Stay out of the spring head itself","Pack out everything, because there is no current to carry it away"}',
  '{"Do not feed or touch manatees, and never approach a calf","Do not swim above the spring pool, where the current is strong","Do not bring glass into the water"}'),
 ('hawaii',
  '{"Green sea turtles on the sand at almost every beach","Coral reefs that start within a few hundred yards of shore","Warm water all year, from 78F in January to 84F in August"}',
  'No wetsuit. Hawaii runs 78-84F (26-29C) all year, so a rash guard is the most useful thing to bring, for sun rather than for cold.',
  '{"Keep 10 ft (3 m) from green sea turtles","Use reef-safe sunscreen","Respect the Marine Life Conservation District rules posted at each site"}',
  '{"Do not touch or stand on coral","Do not feed fish or turtles","Do not take shells or any marine life"}'),
 ('hawaii/oahu',
  '{"Lanikai Beach''s calm, shallow reef and its turtles","The tide pools at the far east end of the island","Hanauma Bay''s protected coral, for the days you want a guide and a fee"}',
  'No wetsuit: 78-84F (26-29C) all year. Bring a rash guard and a reef shoe for the lava entries at Makapuu.',
  '{"Use a rash guard, because the sun is the real risk on an exposed reef","Keep to the posted swimming areas","Park early at Lanikai, because the lot fills by mid-morning"}',
  '{"Do not enter the Makapuu tide pools alone, because sharks are present","Do not take coral or shells","Do not step on coral to reach a better view"}'),
 ('hawaii/maui',
  '{"Molokini Crater, a sunken volcanic caldera snorkelled by boat","Green turtles at Makena Beach, where the reef runs close to the sand","Calm reef coves at Kapalua and Kuilima"}',
  'No wetsuit: 78-84F (26-29C) all year. A rash guard for the sun, and reef shoes for the lava shelf at Makena.',
  '{"Snorkel Makena at low tide, when the reef is shallow and clear","Keep to the marked swim zones","Book Molokini trips for a calm morning"}',
  '{"Do not land on Molokini, because it is a seabird sanctuary","Do not stand on the coral or take shells","Do not feed the fish"}'),
 ('hawaii/big-island',
  '{"The manta ray night snorkel in Kona","Sea turtles basking at dawn on the black sand at Punaluu","A flooded cave at Kaue, reached on a 2-mile round trip"}',
  'No wetsuit: 78-84F (26-29C) all year. A rash guard and reef shoes for the lava entries are enough.',
  '{"Float at the surface at night and let the mantas come to you","Give turtles space when they are basking","Go to Kealakekua Bay early, because the hike is hot and exposed"}',
  '{"Do not touch the turtles on the black sand","Do not land on the islet at Molokini","Do not take marine life inside the reserves"}')
) as v(path, highlights, wetsuit_note, rules_do, rules_avoid)
where regions.path = v.path;

-- ---------- spots ----------
update spots set
  highlights = v.highlights::text[],
  natural_features = v.natural_features,
  wetsuit_recommendation = v.wetsuit_recommendation,
  water_temp_note = v.water_temp_note,
  rules_do = v.rules_do::text[],
  rules_avoid = v.rules_avoid::text[],
  conservation_note = v.conservation_note
from (values
 ('ahihi-kinau',
  '{"Spinner dolphins in the bay at dawn","Dense coral and 400-year-old colonies","A 35-acre protected reserve you snorkel from shore"}',
  'Lava substrate and a living coral reef in a cove that was closed to fishing in 1972 and became a reserve in 1994.',
  'A rash guard. The water is 77-83F (25-28C) all year and the shallow entry means you will be in and out of the sun.',
  '77-83F (25-28C) all year. The reef warms up fast in the sun, so midday is hottest and the wind picks up after that.',
  '{"Keep to the buoyed swim area","Stay on the sand while you are crossing the shallow reef","Let the spinner dolphins come to you"}',
  '{"Do not touch or stand on the coral","Do not feed the fish or the dolphins","Do not swim in the closed section of the reserve"}',
  'The reserve is managed by the Hawaii Department of Land and Natural Resources, which closes part of it to entry during nesting season. The coral here is some of the oldest in the state and is protected from all take.'),
 ('bill-baggs-cape-florida',
  '{"A shallow, grassy flat with stingrays and rays","Dolphins passing the point in the morning","Easy shore entry with no boats in the water"}',
  'Mangrove shoreline meeting a shallow sand and seagrass flat, with the reef starting a short distance out.',
  'A 3mm shorty from December to March, when the Gulf water drops to 70-74F (21-23C). Bare skin is fine in summer.',
  '70-84F (21-29C). Winter is the cooler end, summer brings storms that stir the flat and cut the visibility.',
  '{"Walk at the waterline and shuffle your feet for stingrays","Watch for dolphins on the way in","Check the tide before you set out"}',
  '{"Do not take any marine life","Do not feed the rays","Do not swim in the posted closure areas"}',
  'The cape sits inside the Florida Keys National Marine Sanctuary, which protects the mangrove fringe and the nearshore flats from anchoring and take.'),
 ('biscayne-national-park',
  '{"Coral heads in 8 to 20 ft of water","Large grouper and barracuda in the open water","Mangrove islands and a shallow bay in the same trip"}',
  'A living coral reef on the edge of the shelf, with hardbottom, patch reef and mangrove shoreline habitats.',
  'A 3mm shorty from December to April, when the water sits at 72-76F (22-24C). Most trips run in summer, when a rash guard is enough.',
  '74-85F (23-29C) in summer, 72-78F (22-26C) in winter.',
  '{"Wear the snorkel vest the crew provides","Stay with the boat and the group","Bring a rash guard and a hat"}',
  '{"Do not feed the fish","Do not touch the coral","Do not take anything from the reef"}',
  'The park protects more than 175 square miles of coral and mangrove. Its Institute runs the guided snorkel trips, and the reefs are monitored by the National Coral Reef Monitoring Program.'),
 ('black-rock',
  '{"A steep black lava point that drops straight down","Reef fish in deep blue water right off the shore","Clear water and a strong current on the best days"}',
  'Volcanic lava point and wall, with a hardbottom reef that starts in a few feet of water and falls away quickly.',
  'A 3mm full suit. The water runs 62-66F (16-19C) most of the year and the wall is deep enough that you will get cold fast.',
  '62-70F (16-21C), coldest in February and March and warmest in August and September.',
  '{"Scramble up the rocks away from the breaking waves and let a set pass before entering","Watch the water and the swell for a clean entry","Keep to the point and do not go around the far side alone"}',
  '{"Do not climb on the wet lava at the wave line","Do not take any marine life","Do not swim alone: the point sets up a rip"}',
  'The point is inside a Marine Life Conservation District, where all marine life is protected from take.'),
 ('camp-cactus',
  '{"Sea lions on the ledges above the water","A kelp bed and rock reef on the east end","Clear water with a drop-off just past the entry"}',
  'Rocky lava shore with kelp and a steep submarine ledge, the habitat for the island''s California sea lion colony.',
  'A 3mm full suit: 60-64F (16-18C) most of the year, and the channel can feel colder still when a swell runs.',
  '60-68F (16-20C), coldest in winter when the Catalina Channel runs its biggest swell.',
  '{"Give the sea lions plenty of space and keep off the ledges","Enter where the rock is lowest and the surge is smallest","Watch for the Channel swell before you commit to the water"}',
  '{"Do not touch or approach the sea lions","Do not take marine life","Do not swim in the kelp if it is breaking, because it can hold you down"}',
  'The south end of Catalina is a Marine Life Conservation District, a no-take reserve run by the California Department of Fish and Wildlife.'),
 ('casino-point-dive-park',
  '{"A shore entry straight onto a sloping reef","Garibaldi and kelp bass in the shallows","Scuba divers and snorkelers sharing one protected patch"}',
  'A rocky reef shelf with kelp and hardbottom, protected as a shore-accessible dive park.',
  'A 3mm full suit: 60-65F (16-18C). Divers on this site wear one in July.',
  '60-68F (16-20C), with the coldest water in January and February.',
  '{"Watch for divers and give them room at the entry","Stay inside the dive park boundaries","Move slowly and keep your hands off the rock"}',
  '{"Do not spearfish or take anything inside the no-take park","Do not feed the fish","Do not swim in the marked boat channel"}',
  'The dive park is a no-take Marine Life Conservation District, which means everything inside it is protected from collection.'),
 ('crandon-park',
  '{"A sandy bottom that stays shallow for a long way out","Stingrays in the shallows and a small reef at the north end","Birds and a wide, uncrowded beach at the south end"}',
  'Sand and seagrass flats with a nearshore patch reef at the north end of the beach.',
  'A rash guard most of the year. A 3mm shorty for December to March, when the water is 72-75F (22-24C).',
  '72-84F (22-29C), with the clearest water and the biggest swell in winter.',
  '{"Stay on the ocean side of the channel markers","Walk on the sand and shuffle your feet for stingrays","Use the free three-hour parking passes from the City of Miami Beach"}',
  '{"Do not take shells or coral","Do not feed the fish","Do not bring glass containers"}',
  'Crandon sits on Key Biscayne, which was the site of the Miami Marine Stadium and is now part of the Crandon Park and Beach natural area, with turtle nesting monitored on the north end.'),
 ('datura-avenue-reef',
  '{"A three-tier natural reef that starts about 100 yards from the beach","Turtles and schooling fish on the first terrace","A reef you can snorkel without ever getting on a boat"}',
  'A living hardbottom reef that steps down in three terraces, with spur-and-groove coral and sand channels between them.',
  'A 3mm shorty from November to March (72-75F / 22-24C). Most people snorkel without one in summer.',
  '72-85F (22-29C), with the clearest water in winter and the warmest in August.',
  '{"Look for the beach portal at the end of Datura Avenue and swim out on the bearing of the markers","Watch for boat traffic and stay out of the channel","Stay on the first terrace if you are not confident in open water"}',
  '{"Do not stand on the coral","Do not take any marine life","Do not snorkel in the marked channel: it is a boat staging area"}',
  'The reef sits inside the Florida Keys National Marine Sanctuary boundary at its northern edge, and the marine archaeological preserve offshore adds a second layer of protection.'),
 ('descanso-beach',
  '{"A calm, sandy shoreline under the Palos Verdes cliffs","Sea lions on the rocks near the beach club","Open water views toward the Channel Islands"}',
  'Sand and rock shore with kelp beds and rocky reef close to shore, backed by a bluff.',
  'A 3mm shorty: the water runs 62-68F (16-20C). Divers wear a full suit year-round.',
  '62-70F (16-21C), coldest in February, warmest in September.',
  '{"Watch for the marine mammals resting on the rocks and keep your distance","Snorkel away from the main swim zone for more wildlife","Check the surf before you go in"}',
  '{"Do not take any marine life","Do not feed the sea lions","Do not swim near the rock outcrops where they haul out"}',
  'Descanso Beach is next to the Palos Verdes Marine Life Conservation District, which protects the kelp and rock habitat just offshore.'),
 ('dry-tortugas-national-park',
  '{"The clearest water in the continental United States","The intact coral of the Florida reef, with drop-offs","More than 300 wrecks, and an 1800s brick fort"}',
  'The Florida reef at its most intact: coral, spur-and-groove and a reef wall that drops into deep blue water.',
  'A 3mm shorty from November to March. The water is 72-76F (22-24C) in winter and 84-88F (29-31C) in summer, and there is no shade for hours.',
  '72-88F (22-31C). The season does not change the water temperature much; it changes the swell.',
  '{"Fly a dive flag","Carry at least a gallon of water per person and use the shade on the island","Stay on the marked trails and off the fort walls"}',
  '{"Do not collect marine life or coral","Do not touch the fort walls or any artefact","Do not swim in the moat: American crocodiles live there"}',
  'Dry Tortugas became a national park in 1937 and its waters are a marine sanctuary. The fort and the wrecks are protected as cultural resources, and the American crocodile population here is one of the northernmost in the range.'),
 ('electric-beach',
  '{"Night snorkel on a kelp forest","Bio-luminescent plankton in the water on some nights","A long open-water swim from the sandy beach"}',
  'Sand bottom dropping to a rocky reef and kelp, the classic La Jolla night snorkel site.',
  'A 3mm full suit and usually a hood: the water is 60-64F (16-18C) and it feels colder at night.',
  '60-68F (16-20C). Night snorkelling is best on a warm, calm evening.',
  '{"Snorkel with a buddy and never alone","Use a float, because the swim out to the reef is long","Carry a waterproof torch"}',
  '{"Do not touch the kelp","Do not take marine life","Do not swim in the rip near the shore break"}',
  'The kelp forest off Electric Beach is one of the most studied in Southern California, and the city of San Diego protects it as a marine reserve with no take.'),
 ('emerald-reef',
  '{"A coral reef in deep, clear water","Sharks, rays and big fish in blue water","A site that rewards a boat snorkel"}',
  'Deep reef habitat off a ledge, with a clean wall and open blue water.',
  'A 3mm full suit, and a hood if you are staying in the water for a while: 62-68F (16-20C).',
  '62-72F (16-22C), warmest in late summer.',
  '{"Fly a dive flag and keep it above the surface","Watch for current, which runs along the ledge","Stay with the boat and tell someone your plan"}',
  '{"Do not take marine life","Do not feed the fish","Do not touch the reef"}',
  'The Emerald Reef is a submerged reef off the San Diego coast that boaters know for its clear water and pelagic life.'),
 ('fanning-springs',
  '{"A clear 72F spring run you can swim for a mile","Manatees that gather in the cooler months","A deep spring bowl fed by 65 million gallons a day"}',
  'A limestone spring that discharges into the Suwannee River, with a deep bowl, a shaded river run and cypress and oak on the banks.',
  'No wetsuit. The water holds 72F (22C) all year. If you are cold-sensitive, bring a 1mm suit.',
  '68-72F (20-22C) all year, because the water comes from the aquifer and never sees sunlight.',
  '{"Use a float and a snorkel in the river run","Keep to the river and stay clear of the spring head","Swim with the current on the way out and against nothing on the way back"}',
  '{"Do not swim in the spring bowl: it is protected and the current is dangerous","Do not feed or touch manatees","Do not bring glass into the water"}',
  'Fanning Springs is one of the largest springs in the world by discharge, and its manatee population is monitored by the FWC and by Georgia State University research crews.'),
 ('gilchrist-blue-springs',
  '{"A short, clear swim in 68-70F water","A spring run that leads straight to the Santa Fe River","Turtles, fish and cypress shaded water"}',
  'A limestone spring with a deep pool at the head, a short run and the Santa Fe River 200 yards downstream.',
  'No wetsuit. The water holds 68-70F (20-21C) all year.',
  '68-70F (20-21C) year-round. Visibility drops sharply after heavy rain, which brings tannin into the run.',
  '{"Swim the run rather than the pool, where the current is stronger","Park in the free lot and walk in","Go on a weekday, when the pool is quiet"}',
  '{"Do not swim above the spring pool, where the current is strong","Do not take shells or any marine life","Do not bring glass"}',
  'Gilchrist Blue Springs is part of the Gilchrist County Springs system, and the Santa Fe River below it is a Wild and Scenic River with its own protection.'),
 ('hanauma-bay',
  '{"A 2,000-year-old coral reef inside a volcanic crater","Green sea turtles on the reef in the first years","A shallow inner bay that beginners can walk into"}',
  'A fringing coral reef on the rim of a sunken crater, with a protected inner bay and a deep outer basin.',
  'No wetsuit. The water is 77-83F (25-28C) all year, and the bay is hot and shallow, so a rash guard matters more than warmth.',
  '77-83F (25-28C) year-round, with the warmest months running a few degrees higher.',
  '{"Watch the mandatory reef-protection film before you go in","Stay inside the inner bay if you are a beginner","Keep 10 ft (3 m) from turtles and keep your hands off the reef"}',
  '{"Do not touch or stand on the coral","Do not feed any animal","Do not use non-reef-safe sunscreen"}',
  'Hanauma Bay was closed for 25 years from 1990 and reopened in 2000 with a paid reservation system, strict rules and a funded education and restoration programme.'),
 ('honolua-bay',
  '{"A deep, clear reef pool with a coral wall","Dense fish schools in a sheltered cove","A Marine Life Conservation District with no take at all"}',
  'A rocky inlet with a coral reef on the outer wall and a sheltered sandy pool inside.',
  'A rash guard in summer. A 3mm shorty for the winter months, when the water drops to 72-74F (22-23C).',
  '72-80F (22-27C), coldest in February and March, warmest in August and September.',
  '{"Check the surf and the swell before entering, because the bay breaks hard in winter","Stay on the rock and the sand edge and move out on the reef","Use reef shoes for the entry"}',
  '{"Do not take any marine life: it is an MLCD","Do not touch the coral","Do not feed the fish"}',
  'Honolua Bay is one of the oldest Marine Life Conservation Districts in Hawaii, established in 1953, which makes it one of the earliest no-take areas in the state.'),
 ('john-pennekamp-state-park',
  '{"The reef that starts right at the sand","Coral heads, turtles and the clearest water in the Keys","A glass-bottom boat trip if you would rather stay dry"}',
  'The Florida reef at its northern start point: hardbottom, coral heads and a spur-and-groove reef that runs parallel to the shore.',
  'A 3mm shorty from November to March, when the water is 72-76F (22-24C). A rash guide in summer.',
  '73-85F (23-29C), with the clearest water in late summer and early autumn.',
  '{"Fly a dive flag: it is required by state law for snorkelers as well as divers","Stay on the marked snorkel trail","Take a towel and a cover-up, because the boat ride is as much of the day as the snorkel"}',
  '{"Do not spearfish anywhere in the park","Do not take coral or marine life","Do not swim outside the marked snorkel trail"}',
  'The park was created in 1959 as the world''s first undersea park, and the reef tract it protects runs about 21 miles out to the edge of the continental shelf.'),
 ('kahaluu-beach-park',
  '{"A green turtle pool right at the shore","Two freshwater springs that meet the ocean","A marked swim zone with a lifeguard and a boater boundary"}',
  'A sand and lava shoreline with coral close in and a freshwater spring surfacing under the reef.',
  'A rash guard. The water is 77-83F (25-28C) all year and the shore entry is shallow, so sun is the only thing to dress for.',
  '77-83F (25-28C) year-round.',
  '{"Stay inside the marked swim zone, which is buoyed and watched by lifeguards","Shuffle your feet in the sand for stingrays","Keep 10 ft (3 m) from the turtles"}',
  '{"Do not stand on the coral","Do not feed the turtles","Do not swim past the buoys into the boat channel"}',
  'Kahaluu is a Marine Life Conservation District and a Hawaii Marine Laboratory Refuge, and the turtles here are habituated to people but still protected.'),
 ('kapalua-bay',
  '{"A calm, sandy beach with a reef on one side","Turtles resting on the sand","Easy entry for the whole family"}',
  'Sand beach with a fringing reef to the north and a rocky point to the south.',
  'A rash guard. The water is 77-83F (25-28C) all year.',
  '77-83F (25-28C) year-round, and calmest in the early morning.',
  '{"Snorkel the reef to the north of the beach access","Walk on the sand to avoid the shallow reef","Keep your distance from resting turtles"}',
  '{"Do not stand on the coral","Do not take shells","Do not feed the fish"}',
  'The Kapalua area includes a Marine Life Conservation District, so all marine life in the coves is protected from take.'),
 ('kealakekua-bay',
  '{"A freshwater bay and an ancient heiau on the shore","Coral in the last bay, on the edge of a drowned valley","A hike in, with no road to the water"}',
  'A drowned river valley with coral in the protected interior bay, surrounded by lava rock and old settlement sites.',
  'A rash guard. The water is 77-83F (25-28C) all year.',
  '77-83F (25-28C) year-round, and the bay is often calmer in the morning.',
  '{"Hike in early: the 2-mile round trip is exposed and there is no shade","Pack out everything, including what you brought in","Stay on the trail past the heiau, which is a cultural site"}',
  '{"Do not touch or take anything from the heiau or the burial caves","Do not take coral","Do not land a kayak without a state permit"}',
  'The bay contains the Puʻuwai heiau, a sacred site that is protected, and the shoreline is a state historic site with its own rules.'),
 ('ko-olina-lagoons',
  '{"A calm, shallow lagoon with fish that never leave","Green turtles resting on the sand inside the breakwater","No current and no boat traffic"}',
  'A man-made coastal lagoon of shallow sand, rock and coral, separated from the open ocean by a rock breakwater.',
  'A rash guard. The water is 77-83F (25-28C) all year and the lagoon never gets deep.',
  '77-83F (25-28C) year-round.',
  '{"Stay inside the lagoon, because the currents outside the breakwater openings are strong","Keep off the rocks near the openings","Walk on the sand to avoid the shallow coral"}',
  '{"Do not take coral or shells","Do not feed the fish","Do not climb on the breakwater"}',
  'The lagoons were built to restore fish habitat and they are managed as a refuge where fish can grow without being caught.'),
 ('kona-manta-night-snorkel',
  '{"Manta rays up to 20 ft wing span, in a group of five or six","A night plankton feed that brings them to the surface","A coral garden lit by torchlight on the way home"}',
  'Open coastal water over a deep reef flat, with coral bommies and the manta aggregation feeding on plankton at the surface.',
  'No wetsuit: 77-83F (25-28C) all year. A warm layer for after, because the night air drops fast after sunset.',
  '77-83F (25-28C) all year, and the water is often warmer than the air at night.',
  '{"Float on your back and keep your hands to yourself","Keep your torch off the mantas","Stay with the group and follow the light board"}',
  '{"Do not touch the mantas","Do not chase them or try to guide them","Do not use flash photography"}',
  'The Hawaiian manta population is monitored by the National Marine Fisheries Service, and the operators work with researchers who identify individuals by their belly patterns.'),
 ('kuilima-cove',
  '{"A wide, calm sand beach inside the outer reef","Fish held in by the reef","Sunsets over the water with no crowd"}',
  'A pocket of sand and coral reef protected by an outer reef line, with a shallow shore break.',
  'A rash guard. The water is 77-83F (25-28C) all year.',
  '77-83F (25-28C) year-round.',
  '{"Stay inside the outer reef, where the water is calmest","Walk on the sand at the shoreline","Snorkel in the morning, when the water is clearest"}',
  '{"Do not take coral or shells","Do not feed the fish","Do not swim outside the reef in the swell"}',
  'The cove sits in a Marine Life Conservation District, where all marine life is protected from take.'),
 ('la-jolla-cove',
  '{"Garibaldi fish and a sea lion colony on the rocks","A kelp forest you can swim right through","The view from the shore that brings people here every day"}',
  'A rocky coastal kelp forest on a shelf of rock and sand, with pinniped haul-out sites above.',
  'A 3mm full suit. La Jolla water runs 60-65F (16-18C) most of the year, and the kelp forest holds the cold in.',
  '60-68F (16-20C), coldest in February and March.',
  '{"Enter at the sandy bottom on the north side, away from the shore break","Keep well back from the resting sea lions","Go on a calm day, when the surge is low"}',
  '{"Do not take any marine life","Do not feed or approach the sea lions","Do not stand on the kelp"}',
  'La Jolla Cove sits inside the La Jolla Marine Reserve and the San Diego Marine Life Conservation District, both of which prohibit all take.'),
 ('la-jolla-sea-caves',
  '{"Sea caves lit from the water","Sea lions in the cave mouth","A kayaker''s view of the kelp canopy"}',
  'Sea caves and a rocky kelp forest in the water off La Jolla.',
  'A 3mm full suit. The water runs 60-65F (16-18C) and the caves hold the cold.',
  '60-68F (16-20C), coldest in winter.',
  '{"Go with a guide: swell surges into the caves","Sit on the outside of the kayak where you can get out fast","Keep your head down and watch for the ceiling in the caves"}',
  '{"Do not touch the cave walls or the marine life","Do not feed the sea lions","Do not go in alone"}',
  'The caves and the kelp around them are inside the San Diego Marine Life Conservation District, a no-take area.'),
 ('la-jolla-shores-leopard-sharks',
  '{"Leopard sharks in the shallow sand from June to October","A student kelp bed protected by a marine reserve","A calm, shallow shore that beginners can use"}',
  'A sand and cobble beach with a rocky kelp bed just offshore, and a protected student reserve on the reef.',
  'A 3mm shorty from June to September, when the water is 64-68F (18-20C). A full suit is more comfortable in the winter.',
  '63-69F (17-21C), coldest in February, warmest in September.',
  '{"Shuffle your feet when you walk on the sand: stingrays bury themselves there","Keep 10 ft (3 m) from the leopard sharks and never touch them","Snorkel in the marked swim zone at Scripps"}',
  '{"Do not take any marine life","Do not touch or stand on the kelp bed","Do not swim off the pier, where rips run around the pilings"}',
  'The kelp bed off La Jolla Shores is a Marine Life Conservation District, and the leopard sharks there are a protected species that is routinely monitored by the Scripps Institution of Oceanography.'),
 ('lanikai-beach',
  '{"A shallow, calm reef that beginners can walk into","Green turtles grazing on the reef","An almost unbroken sand beach with the Mokulua islands offshore"}',
  'A fringing reef of coral heads and sand channels a short way offshore, with a wide sand beach and a shallow inner lagoon.',
  'A rash guard. The water is 77-83F (25-28C) all year, and the reef sits in full sun.',
  '77-83F (25-28C) year-round, and the clearest from late spring to early autumn.',
  '{"Enter near the middle of the beach, where the reef is shallow","Swim with a local if you are not confident, since there is no lifeguard at the Lanikai end","Keep 10 ft (3 m) from the turtles"}',
  '{"Do not take coral or shells","Do not stand on the reef","Do not feed the fish","Pack out everything you carry in"}',
  'Lanikai is a Marine Life Conservation District, and the beach is one of the most heavily used turtle habitat on Oahu, with daily turtle counts run by volunteers.'),
 ('little-eggs-beach',
  '{"A huge swell and a wild, remote feel","Kelp beds and rock in the shallows","A marine mammal rookery closed at the north end"}',
  'Rocky lava shore, kelp forest and deep blue water off the exposed west end of Catalina.',
  'A 3mm full suit, and a hood if you are staying out: the water runs 60-65F (16-18C) and the wind picks up in the afternoon.',
  '60-68F (16-20C), with the biggest swell from November to March.',
  '{"Watch the swell before you enter, because it runs hard here","Stay on the trail and keep clear of the rookery fence","Go with a buddy: the current can build quickly"}',
  '{"Do not enter the closed marine mammal rookery","Do not take marine life","Do not swim past the point alone"}',
  'The whole south end of Catalina is a Marine Life Conservation District, and Little Eggs has an additional seasonal closure around the sea lion and seal rookery.'),
 ('lovers-cove',
  '{"A rocky cove with deep blue water and a kelp bed","Sea lions and a resident harbour seal","The clearest water on the island in the afternoon"}',
  'Rocky cove with a kelp forest and rock reef, with a sandy bottom that drops away quickly.',
  'A 3mm full suit: 60-65F (16-18C). Divers and snorkelers wear one here even in July.',
  '60-70F (16-21C), with the best visibility on a calm afternoon.',
  '{"Enter at the rocky edge on the south side, where the surge is gentler","Give the seal and the sea lions space","Keep your hands off the kelp"}',
  '{"Do not take marine resources","Do not feed the fish, even where it is allowed, because it changes their behaviour","Do not disturb the harbour seal"}',
  'Lovers Cove is inside the Santa Catalina Island Marine Life Conservation District, where fishing for take is restricted and the kelp forest is protected.'),
 ('makapuu-tide-pools',
  '{"Natural tide pools at the edge of the Pacific","Sharks in the open water just beyond the reef","A remote shore with no services and no crowds"}',
  'Basalt lava shelves cut into tide pools, with a fringing reef and deep blue water on the seaward side.',
  'A rash guard. The water is 77-83F (25-28C) all year; you will be out of the water in the sun most of the time.',
  '77-83F (25-28C) year-round, and the pools hold water at every tide.',
  '{"Go at low tide and read the posted rules before you enter","Never swim here alone: tiger sharks and oceanic whitetip are present","Stay on the lava shelf and off the coral"}',
  '{"Do not take marine life or spearfish","Do not touch or stand on the coral","Do not swim past the reef line"}',
  'Makapuu is inside the Waimanalo Marine Life Conservation District, so all marine life is protected from take, and the tide pools are fragile habitat that breaks easily.'),
 ('makena-beach',
  '{"Green turtles resting in the shallows","A shallow lava reef right at the sand","A long, empty beach with no buildings on it"}',
  'A sand beach backed by lava rock, with a shallow fringing reef and an open ocean beyond.',
  'A rash guard. The water is 77-83F (25-28C) all year.',
  '77-83F (25-28C) year-round. Winter swells are noticeably calmer on this side of the island.',
  '{"Snorkel in the morning, when the water is calmest and the reef is clear","Use reef shoes over the lava rock","Keep 10 ft (3 m) from resting turtles"}',
  '{"Do not remove coral, rocks or shells","Do not drive onto the sand","Pack out all rubbish"}',
  'Makena is on the coast of a protected stretch of Maui, and the turtles here rest on the reef in the shallows, so the beach is monitored during nesting season.'),
 ('maluaka-turtle-town',
  '{"Turtles resting on the sand in a small cove","A rocky, lava-lined shore","Easy snorkelling from the beach"}',
  'A rocky lava shoreline with a shallow reef and sandy pockets, the traditional turtle resting area on Maui.',
  'A rash guard. The water is 77-83F (25-28C) all year.',
  '77-83F (25-28C) year-round.',
  '{"Give the resting turtles space and never block their route","Snorkel early, before the boat tours arrive","Stay off the lava rock"}',
  '{"Do not touch or crowd the turtles","Do not take shells","Do not feed the fish"}',
  'The turtles here are a well-known population, and the site is a Marine Life Conservation District, so nothing can be taken from it.'),
 ('manatee-springs',
  '{"Wild manatees in the cooler months","A clear spring pool about 70F all year","A river run lined with cypress and a big spring head"}',
  'A limestone spring head discharging into a clear, deep river run, with a boardwalk and an open viewing area.',
  'No wetsuit. The water holds 68-70F (20-21C) all year, so it is a swimsuit rather than a wetsuit day.',
  '68-70F (20-21C) year-round, and clearest in the early morning before wind picks up.',
  '{"Watch from the boardwalk before you get in the water","Stay out of the spring head area, where a floating person can be pulled down","Use a float in the river run"}',
  '{"Do not feed or touch manatees, and never approach a calf","Do not swim directly over the spring head","Do not bring glass into the water"}',
  'Manatee Springs hosts one of the largest concentrations of manatees in Florida, and the state runs a tag-and-release study here through the Florida Fish and Wildlife Research Institute.'),
 ('manoa-bay',
  '{"A shallow fringing reef you can swim over in a few minutes","Spotted eagle rays in the afternoon","Green turtles on the sand in the shallow water"}',
  'A shallow reef shelf of coral and sand, with a sandy shallow bottom and a deeper edge to the north.',
  'A rash guard. The water is 77-83F (25-28C) all year.',
  '77-83F (25-28C) year-round, and clearest in the morning before the afternoon trades bring runoff.',
  '{"Snorkel early, before the wind and the swell","Stay off the coral shelf and keep your fins up","Leave the turtles and rays alone"}',
  '{"Do not stand on the coral shelf","Do not ride, touch or follow the turtles","Do not feed the fish"}',
  'The bay sits inside a Marine Life Conservation District, and the eagle rays and turtles that use it are a monitored population.'),
 ('maunalua-bay',
  '{"A deep, blue boat-only snorkel","Coral outcrops with large fish","Very few people, because it takes a boat"}',
  'A rocky shoreline with coral outcrops just offshore and deep water close by.',
  'A rash guard. The water is 77-83F (25-28C) all year.',
  '77-83F (25-28C) year-round.',
  '{"Fly a dive flag","Stay with the boat and keep an eye on the swell","Watch for current in the deeper sections"}',
  '{"Do not take marine life","Do not feed the fish","Do not touch the coral"}',
  'The bay is surrounded by a Marine Life Conservation District, which protects the coral and the fish that live on it.'),
 ('molokini-crater',
  '{"A submerged volcanic crater, open on one side","Hundreds of fish in one small place","Turtles that come to rest inside the crater"}',
  'A drowned volcanic caldera with a coral rim, steep inner walls and a sandy floor.',
  'A rash guard. The water is 77-83F (25-28C) all year, and the crater walls shade you from the sun.',
  '77-83F (25-28C) year-round.',
  '{"Follow the crew''s briefing about the currents at the crater mouth","Fly a dive flag","Keep your hands off the coral wall"}',
  '{"Do not land on the islet: it is a seabird sanctuary","Do not feed the fish","Do not take marine life"}',
  'Molokini is a state-designated marine life conservation district and a seabird sanctuary, with restoration work and monitoring of the coral and the nesting birds.'),
 ('olowalu',
  '{"A wide, shallow reef you can walk out onto","A long sand beach with a rocky point at the end","An untouched feeling despite being close to town"}',
  'A shallow fringing reef in front of a sand beach, with a rocky point and good visibility in the morning.',
  'A rash guard. The water is 77-83F (25-28C) all year.',
  '77-83F (25-28C) year-round, with visibility that drops in the afternoon as the wind and runoff increase.',
  '{"Snorkel in the morning, when the water is clearest","Go with a buddy, because the reef is shallow and the surf is small","Stay on the sand and off the reef flats"}',
  '{"Do not take coral or shells","Do not feed the fish","Do not collect sand"}',
  'The Olowalu area is part of a Marine Life Conservation District, where the shoreline and reef are protected from take.'),
 ('punaluu-black-sand-beach',
  '{"Green sea turtles basking on the black sand at dawn","A freshwater stream meeting the ocean","A beach made of volcanic cinder"}',
  'A black sand beach of volcanic cinder and lava, with a coral reef just offshore and a freshwater stream running to the sea.',
  'A rash guard. The water is 77-83F (25-28C) all year, and you will be on the sand at sunrise.',
  '77-83F (25-28C) year-round.',
  '{"Arrive before sunrise, which is when the turtles come up","Keep 10 ft (3 m) from the turtles and never block them","Keep the river and the ocean separate, and do not swim in the river pool"}',
  '{"Do not touch, stand on or crowd the turtles","Do not swim in the river pool","Do not take sand or shells"}',
  'Punaluu is a nesting area for green sea turtles, with a turtle protection programme that closes sections of the beach at hatching time and runs daily monitoring.'),
 ('rainbow-springs',
  '{"A 5 to 18 ft deep spring pool at 72F all year","A 400 ft cave you cannot swim into","A white sand bottom in water you can see across"}',
  'A karst spring with a deep, clear pool, a white sand bottom and a collapse cave beside it, fed by the Floridan aquifer.',
  'No wetsuit. The water holds 72F (22C) all year, so it is comfortable for swimming in summer and winter alike.',
  '68-72F (20-22C) all year, with the clearest water in the early morning.',
  '{"Snorkel the pool rather than the cave, which is closed to swimmers","Wear shoes for the walk down, because the path is rough","Go on a weekday, when the crowd is smaller"}',
  '{"Do not enter the cave","Do not swim in the river above the spring","Do not bring glass into the water"}',
  'Rainbow Springs is one of the largest first-magnitude springs in Florida, and its cave and pool are habitat for the Florida cave crayfish and for the green turtle population that uses the spring run.'),
 ('reefline-miami-beach',
  '{"A nearshore reef line right along the beach","Shallow, clear water for a swim","Sunrise and sunset over the water line"}',
  'A shallow sand and rubble bottom with a nearshore hardbottom reef line, typical of the Miami Beach shore.',
  'A rash guard. The water is 74-84F (23-29C) in summer and 72-76F (22-24C) in winter.',
  '72-84F (22-29C), clearest in the morning.',
  '{"Snorkel at high tide, when the reef is covered and clearer","Watch the jet skis and the boats offshore","Keep out of the channel"}',
  '{"Do not take shells or coral","Do not feed the fish","Do not swim in the boat lanes"}',
  'The nearshore reef is part of the Florida Keys National Marine Sanctuary boundary and is protected from anchoring and take.'),
 ('sand-key-lighthouse',
  '{"A historic lighthouse on a tiny sand island","Shallow reef with good fish life","Almost no one else on the water"}',
  'A low sand islet with a shallow reef platform around it, a rock breakwater and a coral head on the south side.',
  'A rash guard. The water is 78-85F (26-29C) in summer and 73-76F (23-24C) in winter.',
  '73-85F (23-29C), with the calmest water and the clearest visibility in summer.',
  '{"Carry a dive flag","Take water and sun protection, because the islet has no shade and no freshwater","Stay clear of the surf line around the sand"}',
  '{"Do not take marine life","Do not touch the historic lighthouse","Do not stand on the reef"}',
  'Sand Key Light has been on the National Register of Historic Places since 1989, and the islet and its surrounding reef sit inside the Florida Keys National Marine Sanctuary.'),
 ('scripps-pier',
  '{"A kelp bed and tidepool reef just below the pier pilings","Leopard sharks in the summer shallows","A working pier with pelicans and sea lions on it"}',
  'Rocky reef and kelp in the shallows, with the pilings of the pier covered in marine growth.',
  'A 3mm shorty from June to September, when the water is 64-68F (18-20C). A full suit in the winter.',
  '63-69F (17-21C), coldest in February and warmest in September.',
  '{"Snorkel at high tide, when the tidewalk runs for about two hours either side of it","Stay in the posted swim zone, which is watched by lifeguards","Shuffle your feet in the sand for stingrays"}',
  '{"Do not swim off the pier: rips run around the pilings","Do not touch the pilings or the life on them","Do not take any marine life"}',
  'The reef under the pier is a Marine Life Conservation District, and Scripps Institution of Oceanography runs long-term monitoring of the leopard shark aggregation in the summer.'),
 ('seven-mile-bridge-wreck',
  '{"Concrete bridge stumps standing in clear water","Barnacles and coral growth on the old piers","A heritage trail on the new bridge above you"}',
  'The concrete stumps and cutwaters of the 1912 Overseas Railway bridge, standing in shallow water on a sand and rubble bottom.',
  'A rash guard. The water is 74-84F (23-29C) in summer and 72-76F (22-24C) in winter.',
  '72-84F (22-29C), and the water is clearest in the winter.',
  '{"Keep clear of the current bridge piers and never dive under them","Stay on the outer face of the stumps, where the current is lighter","Bring a mask that will not leak, because the structure is jagged"}',
  '{"Do not take anything from the structure","Do not cut or loosen barnacles","Do not touch the new bridge piers"}',
  'The old bridge is part of the Overseas Railroad Heritage Trail and the Florida Keys National Marine Sanctuary protects the structure and the marine life growing on it.'),
 ('sharks-cove',
  '{"Turtles resting in a small rocky bay","A rocky lava entry into clear water","No crowds, even on a busy Oahu day"}',
  'A small bay with lava rock and shallow reef, with a sandy bottom in places and deep blue water close by.',
  'A rash guard. The water is 77-83F (25-28C) all year.',
  '77-83F (25-28C) year-round, and the bay is calmest in summer.',
  '{"Use reef shoes for the sharp lava at the entry","Go in the morning, before the swell builds","Keep 10 ft (3 m) from the turtles"}',
  '{"Do not take marine life inside the MLCD","Do not stand on the rock or the coral","Do not feed the fish"}',
  'The cove sits inside the Waimanalo Marine Life Conservation District, which protects the reef and the turtles that rest in it.'),
 ('shipwreck-snorkel-trail',
  '{"The anchor, five cannon and a ballast pile at 10 ft","Yellow marker buoys that lead you along the trail","Clear water over a flat rubble bottom"}',
  'A man-made snorkel trail over the debris field of the SS Copenhagen, on a flat rubble and sand bottom with low relief coral.',
  'A 3mm shorty from November to March, when the water is 72-75F (22-24C). Most people snorkel without one in summer.',
  '72-84F (22-29C), with the clearest water in winter.',
  '{"Follow the paired yellow marker buoys and stay with them","Keep to the shallow bottom and do not dive below the trail","Give way to boats and stay clear of the marked channel"}',
  '{"Do not touch the wreck pieces, the cannon or the anchor","Do not take any artefact or marine life","Do not snorkel in the marked channel"}',
  'The trail was dedicated in 2002 by Jean-Michele Cousteau with the Marine Archaeological Council, a nonprofit he inspired to protect Florida shipwrecks. The site sits next to the Florida Underwater Archaeological Preserve of the SS Copenhagen.'),
 ('ss-copenhagen',
  '{"The most intact wooden wreck in Florida waters","Large coral growth on the hull and the debris field","Sargassum, barracuda and large fish in open water"}',
  'A deep-water debris field with the wooden hull of a ship broken in two, covered in hardbottom coral growth, in open coastal water.',
  'A 3mm full suit, and this is a dive site rather than a snorkel site: the wreck sits in about 25 ft of water.',
  '72-84F (22-29C), with visibility usually best in summer.',
  '{"Watch for boat traffic: the site sits outside the protected swim zone","Stay on the surface on the first dive and find the site from there","Fly a dive flag"}',
  '{"Do not touch, do not move and do not remove anything","Do not spearfish: it is prohibited inside the preserve","Do not enter the protected zone from the surface without a boat"}',
  'The SS Copenhagen was declared a Florida Underwater Archaeological Preserve in 1994. Within a preserve it is unlawful to damage, remove or alter the site, which is why the coral on the wreck is one of the oldest measured on a Florida shipwreck.'),
 ('sunset-cliffs-marine-reserve',
  '{"A kelp forest under the bluffs","Rock and sand shelves full of fish","Sea lions on the rocks near the beach"}',
  'Rocky shore and a sheltered kelp forest, with sand channels and a rocky reef under the sandstone cliffs.',
  'A 3mm full suit: the water runs 62-67F (16-19C), and it is warmer in the kelp but colder in the open.',
  '62-70F (16-21C), coldest in February and March.',
  '{"Enter from the rocks at the north end, where the surge is gentler","Keep a wide berth from the seals and sea lions on the beach","Go in the morning, when the surf is smallest"}',
  '{"Do not take marine life inside the reserve","Do not walk on the kelp or the rock","Do not swim in a rip current"}',
  'The reserve was created in 1972 and covers the kelp forest and rocky habitat under the Sunset Cliffs bluffs, with no take and no anchoring in the kelp.'),
 ('turtle-canyon',
  '{"A coral canyon you can swim along","Turtles resting on the coral below","A boat-only site with clear, deep water"}',
  'A coral ridge and canyon system on the outer reef, with vertical walls and ledges covered in coral.',
  'A rash guard. The water is 77-83F (25-28C) all year.',
  '77-83F (25-28C) year-round.',
  '{"Use the flotation the crew provides","Stay with the group, because the current runs along the canyon","Fly a dive flag"}',
  '{"Do not take marine life","Do not touch the coral walls","Do not feed the fish"}',
  'Turtle Canyon is one of the most-visited snorkel sites in Hawaii and is inside a Marine Life Conservation District, so all marine life is protected.'),
 ('two-step',
  '{"Two submerged lava steps and a rocky shoreline","A marked swim area with a lifeguard on the beach","Clean water and deep blue close to shore"}',
  'Lava ledges stepping down into deep water, with reef and sand patches and a rocky shoreline.',
  'A rash guard. The water is 77-83F (25-28C) all year.',
  '77-83F (25-28C) year-round, and calmest in the early morning.',
  '{"Enter at the ramp and step carefully over the lava ledges","Watch for boats loading at the ramp and keep clear of the loading zone","Snorkel in the morning, before the trade winds"}',
  '{"Do not enter the water at Keoneele Cove inside the park","Do not take marine life","Do not use the park restrooms to change or rinse off"}',
  'The area is part of the Kona Coast State Historic Park, and Keoneele Cove at the end of the trail is a cultural site with its own restrictions.'),
 ('waialea-bay',
  '{"A shallow bay with a sandy bottom","Turtles in the shallows at the north end","A quiet alternative to the busier north coast spots"}',
  'A sand and shallow reef bay with a rocky point and a small fringing reef.',
  'A rash guard. The water is 77-83F (25-28C) all year.',
  '77-83F (25-28C) year-round, and the bay is calmest in the morning.',
  '{"Snorkel the reef at the north end of the bay","Walk on the sand where the bottom is shallow","Give the turtles space"}',
  '{"Do not take coral or shells","Do not feed the fish","Do not stand on the reef"}',
  'The bay is in a Marine Life Conservation District, where all marine life is protected from take, and the turtles here rest in the shallow water.'),
 ('wailea-beach',
  '{"A rocky reef shelf on the south shore","A long, quiet sandy beach","Clear water with a lot of coral within reach"}',
  'A rocky reef platform running along a sand beach, with coral outcrops and a shallow inner shelf.',
  'A rash guard. The water is 77-83F (25-28C) all year.',
  '77-83F (25-28C) year-round, with the calmest conditions from autumn through spring.',
  '{"Snorkel the reef along the south shore, and stay off the shallow coral","Use reef shoes where the rock comes close to the surface","Snorkel in the morning"}',
  '{"Do not take coral or shells","Do not bring glass containers","Pack out rubbish"}',
  'The south shore of Maui is lined with resort beaches and protected reef, and the coral here is monitored by the Coral Reef Institute for the West Hawaii reefs.')
) as v(slug, highlights, natural_features, wetsuit_recommendation, water_temp_note, rules_do, rules_avoid, conservation_note)
where spots.slug = v.slug;

-- The Marine Room restaurant sits at the south end of La Jolla Shores Beach and is
-- the usual landmark for the leopard shark swim, so people search for it by name.
update spots set
  alt_names = v.alt_names::text[]
from (values
 ('la-jolla-shores-leopard-sharks','{"La Jolla Shores Beach","Marine Room","Shell Beach","Marine Room Beach"}')
) as v(slug, alt_names)
where spots.slug = v.slug;
